# Change Alt sends the guided "change altitude" MISSION_ITEM with the box's number, decimals dropped.
#
# modifyandSetAlt_Click: `int newalt = (int) Value; setNewWPAlt(new Locationwp {alt = newalt /
# multiplieralt})` - a float MISSION_ITEM, sequence 0, command 16, frame 3 (relative), current 3,
# x and y zero. 25.9 in the box is 25 on the wire. SITL acknowledges it with MISSION_ACK, which the
# link does not log outside a transfer, so the assertion is on what was sent.
# `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:4513-4524, ExtLibs/ArduPilot/Mavlink/MAVLinkInterface.cs:4470-4481`
#
# Needs SITL: tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-changealt.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 5

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

click fly-alt-value
key ctrl+u
type 25.9
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
click fly-changealt
expect fly.sent MISSION_ITEM seq=0 cmd=16 frame=3 current=3 x=0 y=0 z=25
